Bundled datasets and vocabularies:

  - Vocabularies bundled in frontend/public/vocab/. The web UI serves them at
    /vocab/, and the server compiles them in and seeds them as public reference
    models. The per-file title, version, source, copyright holder, licence URI
    and changes are in frontend/public/vocab/NOTICE.md (served at
    /vocab/NOTICE.md), which also reproduces the licence texts that must travel
    with the files. The server records each seeded copy's licence and
    attribution as registry metadata, returned by /api/models (attribution),
    and a download of a seeded copy starts with the file's header as comments,
    then a line saying whether the content is that file's triples, unchanged,
    or a copy that may have been modified in the registry (imbor.ttl: Link
    headers only). The seeded graphs hold each file's triples, which the
    seeder checks against the file. The store writes typed literals in its
    canonical form, with the same values: some xsd:nonNegativeInteger
    literals in dcat.ttl, dcat/2.0.0.ttl, prov.ttl, time.ttl, vcard.ttl,
    ssn.ttl, bibo.ttl, saref.ttl and locn.ttl read as xsd:integer, and two
    +00:00 time zones in pav.ttl read as Z. imbor.ttl has no typed literals and
    is held exactly. The registry publishes no content in the IMBOR entry other
    than that file; a stored copy that no longer matches it is kept as a
    private version served only to those who may write the entry, and the
    file's triples are restored. 17 files came through the Linked Open Vocabularies (LOV)
    corpus snapshot of 2025-12-18 (https://lov.linkeddata.es/), which
    re-serialized them as Turtle; LOV's CC BY 4.0 covers LOV's catalogue and
    does not relicense them. Open Triplestore added a comment header to every
